{
  "id": "graph/synapses",
  "title": "a synapse joins two sessions that talked, from Orca messages and recorded links: one-way or two-way with the count of each direction and the last time, run: and dispatch: addresses resolved to terminals, and never any message content",
  "source": [
    "intended: docs/decisions.md, release 2 of the communication plan; orca orchestration inbox, run-list and worker-list --help for the call shapes"
  ],
  "intent": "A message to run:<id> belongs to the terminal that coordinates the run (run-list), and a dispatch:<id> address to the terminal of that worker (worker-list --run, asked only when the other end is a session of the snapshot). A heartbeat is no talk; a message to oneself, to a session that is not shown or from an address that does not resolve makes no edge; a link to a closed launch that is not shown makes none. Only direction, count and last time leave the message store: subject, body and payload appear in no output and no file.",
